{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>When he is sold to you.</b> Through others — the court sold him for his theft — the verse speaks. But has it not already been said, ״When you buy a Hebrew slave״, and there too the verse speaks of one sold by the court? Rather, because two matters are newly taught here: one, that it writes <b>or a Hebrewess</b> — she too goes free in the sixth year. And not that the court sold her, for a woman is not sold for her theft, as it is said ״for his theft״ and not ״for her theft״ — but a minor girl whom her father sold, and it teaches here that if six years elapsed before she develops signs [of puberty], she goes free. And further, it newly teaches here <b>you shall furnish him liberally</b>."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:13.134851048Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}